<%# An operator's sections, rendered.
  
  ONE DISPATCHER, AND IT CANNOT RENDER A PARTIAL THAT DOES NOT EXIST: `Marketing::SectionSchema.coerce` drops
  any section whose type is not in TYPES before the row is saved, and TYPES is the list of partials in this
  directory. So a malformed section is impossible here rather than guarded against.

  Every string a section carries is rendered escaped. Bodies are plain text by design -- the schema module
  gives the full reasoning, which comes down to this repository having already shipped a stored XSS through a
  Markdown path.
%>
<% Array(sections).each do |section| %>
  <%= render "marketing/sections/#{section['type']}", section: section, page: page %>
<% end %>
